        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioner's fundamental contention is that once a State issues a determination of best available control technology so labeled, no matter how arbitrary, factually unsupported, or unreasoned it may be, the Federal Government has no enforcement authority under the act to take actions to stop the invalid permit from taking effect."
    },
